# LOAD-BEARING. Do not remove.
#
# The saved messages are stored with CRLF line endings, because that is what the
# mail format actually uses. Git's end-of-line translation would rewrite them on
# checkout on some platforms, which changes the bytes of the file.
#
# One graded value in this lab is a SHA-256 digest of an attachment decoded out
# of case03. Base64 decoding ignores line breaks, so that particular digest
# survives translation - but the message files themselves would differ between a
# Windows and a Linux student, and anything that compares them byte-for-byte
# would disagree for no good reason. Marking them binary removes the whole class
# of problem.
#
# Verify with:  git check-attr text -- env/analyst/cases/case01.eml
#               (expect: text: unset)
*.eml -text
